    "question": "A bathroom has 10 6 inch tiles along its width and 20 6 inch tiles along its length.  What is the square footage of the bathroom?",
    "gold": "50",
    "answer": "There are 10 tiles that are 6 inches long running the width of the bathroom so it is 10*6 = <<10*6=60>>60 inches long\nThere are 12 inches in a foot and it’s 60 inches wide so it is 60/12 = 5 feet wide\nThere are 20 tiles that are 6 inches long running the length of the bathroom so it’s 20*6 = <<20*6=120>>120 inches long\nThere are 12 inches in a foot and it’s 120 inches long so it is 120/12 = <<120/12=10>>10 feet wide\nThe square footage is l x w so the bathroom has 10*5 = <<10*5=50>>50 sq feet\n#### 50"
  },
  "generation": {
    "text": "To find the square footage of the bathroom, we need to determine the area of the bathroom in square inches and then convert that area to square feet. Here are the steps:\n\n1. **Calculate the width of the bathroom in inches:**\n   The width of the bathroom is given as 10 tiles, and each tile is 6 inches wide.\n   \\[\n   \\text{Width} = 10 \\times 6 = 60 \\text{ inches}\n   \\]\n\n2. **Calculate the length of the bathroom in inches:**\n   The length of the bathroom is given as 20 tiles, and each tile is 6 inches long.\n   \\[\n   \\text{Length} = 20 \\times 6 = 120 \\text{ inches}\n   \\]\n\n3. **Calculate the area of the bathroom in square inches:**\n   The area of a rectangle is given by the product of its length and width.\n   \\[\n   \\text{Area} = \\text{Width} \\times \\text{Length} = 60 \\times 120 = 7200 \\text{ square inches}\n   \\]\n\n4. **Convert the area from square inches to square feet:**\n   There are 144 square inches in a square foot (since \\(12 \\times 12 = 144\\)).\n   \\[\n   \\text{Area in square feet} = \\frac{7200}{144} = 50 \\text{ square feet}\n   \\]\n\nTherefore, the square footage of the bathroom is \\(\\boxed{50}\\).",
